 # Project agent instructions
+
+## Joined two-triangle tire-ribbon override (2026-10-13)
+The owner requests a different tire-mark approach that improves looks and reduces drawing effort. Use four indexed vertices/two triangles with shared immutable per-wheel endpoints, smooth pressure and width changes and analytic rounded groove shading. This supersedes the thirty-vertex faceted mark profile and old cosmetic instance-data layout. Keep the 16384-slot/four-wheel/0.32m sampling budget, approved warm desert pigment, style/intensity functions, original dust, bridge guards, camera and canonical driving/scoring. Preserve concurrent visibility work. See `docs/TIRE_RIBBONS.md` for actual paired desktop drawing costs, scene captures, scoped checkpoint and remaining owner/physical-device acceptance.
 
 ## Trophy wall final visual pass override (2026-10-13)
 The owner requests one more review/refinement of the trophy wall. Retain the alcove composition and laurel silhouette while using smooth charcoal backing, correctly shaded folded relief leaves/rounded stems, shallow raised brand lettering, satin champagne edging and softer warm gallery wash. Bind stone pigments as source colours on both renderers; preserve the requested wall sheen and floor/deck captures, empty award spaces, local cosmetics and canonical handling/scoring. See `docs/TROPHY_WALL_VISUAL_PASS.md` for actual captures/checks, scoped checkpoint and owner/device AAA acceptance.
